by GromNaN at 2026-04-09T21:07:36Z

Shared `$defs` to reduce repetition in generated schemas

All typed nodes now emit \`\$ref\` instead of inline type schemas. The generated schema is organised in two namespaces:

```json
{
  "$defs": {
    "types": {
      "boolean": { "type": "boolean" },
      "integer": { "type": "integer" },
      "param": { "type": "string", "pattern": "^%[^%]+%$" },
      "scalar": { "type": ["boolean", "null", "number", "string"] },
      "object": { "type": "object" },
      ...
    },
    "nodes": {
      "framework": { "$ref": "#/$defs/types/object", "properties": { ... } },
      "security": { ... }
    }
  },
  "properties": {
    "framework": { "$ref": "#/$defs/nodes/framework" },
    "security":  { "$ref": "#/$defs/nodes/security" }
  }
}
```

When `parameterSchemas` are injected (FrameworkBundle), the primitive type defs include `%param%` support:

```json
"boolean": { "anyOf": [{ "type": "boolean" }, { "$ref": "#/$defs/types/param" }] }
```

`ScalarNode` now correctly maps to `scalar` (`string|number|boolean|null`) instead of `variable` (all types including `array` and `object`), fixing overly permissive schemas for scalar prototypes.

