by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-15T08:34:09Z

I went through the five open threads against the current head, running the code rather than reading it. Three are resolved by the April rework and can be closed:

* @mdeboer's draft version point: the dumper now declares `https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema`, where `deprecated` is valid;
* @stof's `BackedEnum` point: backing values are emitted next to the `!php/enum` form;
* the boolean-only nullability special case: `BaseNode::isNullable()` now generalises it, and the object, array and boolean branches consult it.

But the nullability discussion @stof started is only half done. I built a tree with one node of each kind and compared what the node accepts at runtime (`normalize()` then `finalize()`) with what the generated schema says:

```
node                                 runtime(null)   schema
stringNode('s')                      accepted        {"$ref": ".../string"}          too strict
stringNode('s')->treatNullLike('')   accepted        {"$ref": ".../string"}          too strict
integerNode('i')                     REJECTED        {"$ref": ".../integer"}         consistent
integerNode('i')->treatNullLike(0)   accepted        {"$ref": ".../integer"}         too strict
enumNode('e')->values(['a','b'])     REJECTED        {"enum": ["a","b",null]}        too lax
  ... ->values(['a','b',null])       accepted        {"enum": ["a","b",null,null]}   double null
  ... ->enumFqcn(Suit::class)        accepted        {"enum": [...cases..., null]}   consistent
```

Three findings:

* the `string_null`, `integer_null` and `number_null` `$defs` are defined but never referenced: the `StringNode` and `NumericNode` branches do not consult `isNullable()`, unlike their boolean, object and array siblings. With `treatNullLike()`, the IDE would flag `~` as invalid on a node that accepts it;
* `EnumNode` appends `null` to every enum unconditionally. A plain value enum rejects null at runtime (`The value of type "null" is not allowed for path "mode"`), so the schema validates configs the component throws on. When null *is* a declared value it is emitted twice. Only the `enumFqcn` case accepts null implicitly, so the append should be gated on `\in_array(null, $values, true)` or the enum-FQCN case rather than unconditional;
* a plain `StringNode` accepts null at runtime through its `ScalarNode` heritage, while `isNullable()` reports false, since it only looks at `equivalentValues`. So even wiring `isNullable()` into the string branch would not close the gap. That is worth a decision rather than a patch: either `isNullable()` should reflect `validateType()`'s actual null acceptance, or the schema knowingly stays stricter than the runtime for plain scalars, which is arguably the better DX and just deserves a comment saying so.

One note on my harness in case you want to reproduce: `finalize(null)` alone reports `treatNullLike()` nodes as rejecting, because that conversion happens in `normalize()`. The table above runs both phases.

