by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-15T08:47:09Z

I pushed the fixes for my findings above as a commit on top, so both existing authorships stay intact, and resolved the five open threads: three were already answered by the April rework (draft 2020-12, `BackedEnum` backing values, `isNullable()` replacing the boolean special case), and the remaining nullability gaps are closed by the new commit:

* the `StringNode` and `NumericNode` branches now consult `isNullable()`, so the `string_null`, `integer_null` and `number_null` `$defs` are referenced at last;
* `EnumNode` no longer appends `null` unconditionally: it is emitted when null is a declared value or when the node is bound to an enum FQCN, which is the case that accepts and returns null at runtime;
* `BaseNode::isNullable()` no longer counts the identity null mapping the builder registers on every node. That mapping leaves null to be rejected by the type check, so an `integerNode()` without `treatNullLike()` reported nullable while rejecting null.

Two behaviour notes visible in the regenerated `ExampleConfiguration.schema.json`:

* a plain `stringNode()` is now `string_null`, because `StringNodeDefinition` defaults `nullEquivalent` to `''`: writing `~` on such a node is accepted and means the empty string;
* `string_list_default_null`, an `arrayNode()->defaultNull()`, went from `array_null` to `array`: `defaultNull()` resets the null equivalence, and writing `~` explicitly on that node throws `Expected "array", but got "null"`. The schema now matches that.

Every node kind and null-handling combination is asserted against what `normalize()` plus `finalize()` actually accepts; reverting the two source files fails 8 of the test rows. Config is green at 614 tests and the FrameworkBundle compiler tests at 18.

